CAPTURE_HOOK_CRATE:
  path: memory-api/crates/session-capture-hook
  package_name: session-capture-hook
  bin_name(s): copilot-capture-hook -> src/main.rs
  in_workspace_members: no
  deps: memory-api (path = ../memory-api), serde_json = "1", session-api (path = ../session-api), session-workspace-resolver (path = ../session-workspace-resolver), ticket-api (path = ../ticket-api)
  cli_surface: accepts flags `--transcript-path <PATH>`, `--store-root <PATH>`, `--workspace-slug <SLUG>` (default "default"), `--trigger <NAME>` (default "stop"), and `--from-hook-stdin` (causes the binary to read JSON from stdin). When run with `--from-hook-stdin` it reads hook JSON fields `transcript_path`/`transcriptPath`, `workspace_slug`/`workspaceSlug`, `hook_event_name`/`hookEventName`, `tool_use_id`/`toolUseId`, `session_id`/`sessionId`, and `tool_response`/`toolResponse` from stdin. Env vars read: `MCP_MAIN_CHECKOUT` (used to resolve worktree `.session` store root); other runtime workspace info is obtained via `memory_api::workspace::working_dir()`. Outputs: writes captured session data into the resolved session store root (e.g. `.session` under resolved worktree or `--store-root` if provided) via `SessionStoreConfig::capture_copilot_transcript_with_tool_response`; logs to stderr for diagnostics; prints an empty JSON object `{}` to stdout on success. Also probes spill files under the Copilot chat `chat-session-resources/<session_id>/<tool_use_id>` derived from the transcript path.

RESOLVER_CRATE:
  path / package_name / bin_or_lib: memory-api/crates/session-workspace-resolver / session-workspace-resolver / lib (library: `session_workspace_resolver`, path = src/lib.rs)
HOOKS_DIR_FILES: [.github/hooks/hooks.json, .github/hooks/rtk-rewrite.json]
HOOKS_MANIFEST_PATH: .github/hooks/hooks.json
HOOKS_MANIFEST_CONTENT: |
{
  "hooks": {
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "type": "command",
        "command": "copilot-capture-hook --from-hook-stdin",
        "cwd": ".",
        "timeout": 120
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "type": "command",
        "command": "bash tools/agent-hooks/rtk-hook-copilot.sh",
        "cwd": ".",
        "timeout": 5
      },
      {
        "type": "command",
        "command": "bash tools/agent-hooks/preflight-write.sh",
        "cwd": ".",
        "timeout": 30
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "type": "command",
        "command": "bash tools/agent-hooks/validate-docs.sh",
        "cwd": ".",
        "timeout": 30
      },
      {
        "type": "command",
        "command": "bash tools/agent-hooks/terminal-pwd.sh",
        "cwd": ".",
        "timeout": 5
      },
      {
        "type": "command",
        "command": "copilot-capture-hook --from-hook-stdin",
        "cwd": ".",
        "timeout": 120
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "type": "command",
        "command": "copilot-capture-hook --from-hook-stdin",
        "cwd": ".",
        "timeout": 120
      }
    ],
    "SessionEnd": [
      {
        "command": "copilot-capture-hook --from-hook-stdin",
        "cwd": ".",
        "timeout": 120
      }
    ]
  }
}
SCHEMA_NOTES: The manifest maps hook event names to arrays of objects. Each object may include `type` (e.g. "command"), `command` (a shell command string), `cwd` (working directory), and `timeout` (seconds). In `rtk-rewrite.json` there are entries using `bash`/`powershell` keys and `timeoutSec` naming; command values are shell strings (not arg arrays). Schema is permissive/heterogeneous (some entries omit `type`).
